<Layout>
<main>
<section class="hero"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">IoT R&amp;D Engineer · Cloud · Edge · Embedded</div>
  <h1>VENKATESH<br/>BOKKA</h1>
  <p>I build connected systems from device to edge to cloud — with a focus on AWS IoT, Azure IoT, industrial connectivity, Python and embedded platforms.</p>
  <div class="buttons">
    <a class="btn primary" href="#projects">Explore projects</a>
    <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">GitHub ↗</a>
    <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/venkatesh-bokka-983b99126/" target="_blank">LinkedIn ↗</a>
  </div>
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><strong>8+</strong><span>Years engineering</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>AWS</strong><span>IoT &amp; cloud</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>Edge</strong><span>Embedded systems</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>IIoT</strong><span>Industrial connectivity</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="about"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">01 / About</div><h2>Engineering systems that connect.</h2>
  <p class="lead">I work across the full IoT stack: device firmware and gateways, protocols and edge applications, cloud ingestion, APIs, storage and analytics. My goal is to turn device data into reliable, scalable systems.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="skills"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">02 / Technical focus</div><h2>Tools I build with.</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><h3>Cloud &amp; IoT</h3><p>AWS IoT Core, Azure IoT Hub, AWS IoT TwinMaker, Azure Digital Twins, The Things Stack, ChirpStack, Lambda and Azure Functions.</p><span class="tag">AWS</span><span class="tag">Azure</span><span class="tag">Digital twins</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Device Provisioning</h3><p>AWS Fleet Provisioning and claim certificates, Azure DPS with X.509 or symmetric keys, and The Things Stack LoRaWAN OTAA onboarding.</p><span class="tag">Identity</span><span class="tag">Certificates</span><span class="tag">OTAA</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Edge &amp; Embedded</h3><p>ESP32, Raspberry Pi, Arduino, BeagleBone and Linux-based edge systems.</p><span class="tag">ESP32</span><span class="tag">Linux</span><span class="tag">Edge</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Industrial IoT</h3><p>PLC and OPC UA data acquisition with Ignition, Modbus, Mosquitto, Kafka, gateways, telemetry pipelines and device integration.</p><span class="tag">Ignition</span><span class="tag">OPC UA</span><span class="tag">IIoT</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Data Science &amp; Analytics</h3><p>Telemetry feature engineering, anomaly detection and predictive models with AWS and Azure data and ML services.</p><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">ML</span><span class="tag">Analytics</span></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="projects"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">03 / Open-source work</div><h2>From architecture to implementation.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Open-source projects that make the design decisions visible: system boundaries, device flows, cloud services and working code.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><h3>AWS IoT Platform</h3><p>Device connectivity with Fleet Provisioning, claim certificates, JITP/JITR registration, policies, MQTT telemetry and cloud data pipelines.</p><span class="tag">Provisioning</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Azure IoT Platform</h3><p>IoT Hub onboarding through Device Provisioning Service using X.509, symmetric-key or TPM attestation, device twins and routing.</p><span class="tag">DPS</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>IoT Provisioning App</h3><p>Open-source onboarding app for registering devices, generating secure identity material and provisioning AWS IoT, Azure DPS and The Things Stack devices. Repository coming soon.</p><span class="tag">Coming soon</span><span class="tag">Open source</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Digital Twins &amp; 3D</h3><p>Blender-based 3D visualization connected to AWS IoT TwinMaker and Azure Digital Twins for spatial and operational context.</p><span class="tag">Blender</span><span class="tag">3D</span><span class="tag">TwinMaker</span></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>AWS IoT TwinMaker</h3><p>Digital-twin scenes that combine IoT telemetry, equipment relationships and 3D operational context for connected assets.</p><span class="tag">Digital twin</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Azure Digital Twins</h3><p>Model-driven digital twins using Azure Digital Twins, relationships, live property updates and connected-space graphs.</p><span class="tag">Digital twin</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Blender Twin Visualization</h3><p>3D asset and scene workflows in Blender for visualizing devices, facilities and telemetry-driven digital-twin states.</p><span class="tag">Blender</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>The Things Stack</h3><p>LoRaWAN device provisioning with OTAA join credentials, Join Server integration, DevEUI, JoinEUI, AppKey and application data.</p><span class="tag">OTAA</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>ChirpStack</h3><p>Open-source LoRaWAN deployments with device provisioning, MQTT integration, payload handling and monitoring.</p><span class="tag">Open source</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Mosquitto Broker</h3><p>Lightweight open-source MQTT messaging for local development, edge gateways, device testing and telemetry routing.</p><span class="tag">MQTT</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Kafka Event Streaming</h3><p>Durable event streaming for high-volume telemetry, consumer services, integrations and real-time processing.</p><span class="tag">Streaming</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>ESP32 IoT Gateway</h3><p>Embedded gateway experiments connecting sensors and field devices to modern IoT backends.</p><span class="tag">Embedded</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Industrial Edge</h3><p>Edge-first architectures using Linux, Python and Node-RED for protocol integration and local processing.</p><span class="tag">IIoT</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Ignition Industrial Data Platform</h3><p>Reads PLC data through OPC UA into Ignition, sends telemetry to the cloud, stores time-series data, applies machine learning and presents operational dashboards.</p><span class="tag">PLC / OPC UA</span><span class="tag">Machine learning</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>IoT Data Science Platform</h3><p>Processes device telemetry with AWS IoT, Kinesis, S3, Glue, Timestream and SageMaker, alongside Azure IoT Hub, Event Hubs, Data Lake and Azure Machine Learning.</p><span class="tag">AWS</span><span class="tag">Azure</span><span class="tag">Data science</span><a class="card-link" href="https://github.com/venkateshbokka" target="_blank">View repositories ↗</a></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="architecture"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">04 / Architecture to implementation</div><h2>Designed in layers. Delivered in code.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Each project moves from a clear architecture to testable implementation: define the flow, choose the protocol, build the edge path, connect the cloud and document the result.</p>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node">1. Architecture<br/>Sensors / PLC</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">2. Implementation<br/>ESP32 / Python</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">3. Connectivity<br/>LoRaWAN / Mosquitto / REST</div>
  </div>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node">4. Cloud<br/>AWS / Azure / LoRaWAN</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">5. Digital twin<br/>TwinMaker / Azure Digital Twins</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">6. 3D &amp; proof<br/>Blender / Tests / Demo</div>
  </div>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node">PLC / OPC UA<br/>Industrial data</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">Ignition<br/>SCADA / tags</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">Cloud / database<br/>ML / dashboard</div>
  </div>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node">Telemetry<br/>AWS IoT / Azure IoT</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">Data platform<br/>Kinesis / Event Hubs / S3 / Data Lake</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">ML &amp; dashboard<br/>SageMaker / Azure ML / BI</div>
  </div>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node">AWS IoT<br/>Fleet / JITP / JITR</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">Azure DPS<br/>X.509 / key / TPM</div><div class="arrow">→</div>
    <div class="node">The Things Stack<br/>LoRaWAN OTAA</div>
  </div>
</div></section>

